MV-CrystalBench bundles an unmodified subset of upstream CIF, info.json and base.bib files.
Structure constructors expand asymmetric sites using ASE crystal, then standardize
the conventional cell with spglib at 1e-5 angstrom. The generated cell basis, origin
and tiny symmetry idealization can differ from the published CIF representation.
Bond-pair policies, Q2 eligibility decisions, source manifest and scientific tests
are additions made for MV-CrystalBench; they are not AFLOW annotations.

Original papers are cited in each prototype folder base.bib. Library references:
Mehl et al., Computational Materials Science 136, S1-S828 (2017),
doi:10.1016/j.commatsci.2017.01.017.
Hicks et al., Computational Materials Science 199, 110450 (2021),
doi:10.1016/j.commatsci.2021.110450.
Eckert et al., Computational Materials Science 240, 112988 (2024),
doi:10.1016/j.commatsci.2024.112988.
